  "title": "Falling into a pond",
  "question": "Does going in read as hitting water, or as a few dots appearing over a line that never moves?",
  "context_md": "The gnome is a ghost to the CA sweep, so until now a pond answered him with **nothing**: he fell in at terminal velocity and the waterline did not move by one pixel.\n\n- **A** is that, today.\n- **B** throws a crown at the rim, sized by how fast he arrived — a step off a bank gets two droplets, this fall from 40 cells gets twelve.\n\nSame seed, same fall, same frames; the only difference is the effect being on. The water is conserved exactly — every droplet is debited from the pool it came out of.\n\nWhat I am unsure of is **size**: one cell of water per droplet may be too little to read at play zoom. There is a live knob for it (`splash_force` in the PLAYER panel, 0 = off).",
